  "implementation": [
    "Validated CurveFlowLocalRadii stores finite 0 <= inner < outer. Radius pairs accept either order, including zero. Weight is one at/below the inner radius and zero at/above the outer radius; the wall uses t*t*(3-2*t) with t=(outer-distance)/(outer-inner), matching the open-source OpenNURBS localizer polynomial.",
    "Use the existing closest-parameter query on the prepared finite base guide and include the full endpoint distance. Reuse that parameter for the full point map. Return outside points before computing the full deformation; blend coordinates through the existing scale-safe scalar interpolator.",
    "Changing radii clones only morph options and shares prepared guide data. Straight guide pairs retain their existing affine map inside the local blend. Selected grips always use the point map; ordinary Rigid objects use the shared numerical derivative pose.",
    "When a reflected derivative cancels an averaged rigid axis exactly, retain that forward direction while averaging the other axis. Existing orthogonal-frame behavior remains. Qualify reflection cases under three world-axis permutations with native command poses.",
    "Filter outside selected grips before committing while retaining the original grip-owner precedence and group bounds during ordinary staging. Avoid unchanged grip copies and empty history entries. Whole objects still follow Copy even when their geometry is unchanged.",
    "Register Local=Yes|No and LocalRadii=first,second. Require radii before scripted edits. Reuse the Circle getter, drafting plane, point filters/snaps and shared radius-circle painting. Preview, radius changes, cancellation and stale guide invalidation leave the document untouched until one staged commit. Remember the Local toggle but request radii for each new interactive command."
  ],
